{"id": "6b0abc44581c45e1", "schema_version": "0.8", "record_type": "meta", "surveyor": "grok-1", "id_recipe": "sha256('survey-rec|grok-1|' + source_span)[:16]; source_span is L<line> or L<a>-L<b>, letter fragments for multi-record lines", "source_file": "grok-1.md", "source_span": "L800", "section_path": ["from panes", "Latin / IPA / phonetic — mutation sequences (looked at the glyphs)"], "title": "grep-for-NUMBER was the stop — looking at shapes instead", "glyphs": null, "codepoints": null, "axis": "method/self-correction", "direction_note": null, "epistemic_class": "interactive-guided-survey-anecdote", "felt_strength_verbatim": "unstated", "basis": "perceived-directly", "lineage": "unprompted", "constructed": false, "note_verbatim": "I had treated these blocks as letter catalogs and grepped names for NUMBER. That was the stop. Looking at the shapes:", "transcription_confidence": "clear", "migrator_notes": "surveyor's own confession of the name-derived hazard (grepped names for NUMBER, 'that was the stop')", "open": null}
{"id": "edef6854c211e66f", "schema_version": "0.8", "record_type": "generator", "surveyor": "grok-1", "id_recipe": "sha256('survey-rec|grok-1|' + source_span)[:16]; source_span is L<line> or L<a>-L<b>, letter fragments for multi-record lines", "source_file": "grok-1.md", "source_span": "L804", "section_path": ["from panes", "Latin / IPA / phonetic — mutation sequences (looked at the glyphs)", "size of one letter (small → big)"], "title": "size of one letter (small → big)", "glyphs": null, "codepoints": null, "axis": "size of one letter (small → big)", "direction_note": null, "epistemic_class": "interactive-guided-survey-anecdote", "felt_strength_verbatim": "Strong", "basis": "perceived-directly", "lineage": "unprompted", "constructed": false, "note_verbatim": "The same body in a bigger cell. Strong. Each line is its own sequence:\n\nₒ o ᴏ O\nₐ a ᴀ A\nₑ e ᴇ E\nᵢ i ɪ I\nᵤ u ᴜ U\nₙ n ɴ N\nₘ m ᴍ M\nₗ l ʟ L\nₕ h ʜ H\nₚ p ᴘ P\nₜ t ᴛ T\nₛ s S\nₓ x X\nᵒ o O\nª a A\nº o O\n\nTiny raised (ªº) sit at the front of a/o. Subscript (ₒₐₑ…) is another front. Small-cap (ᴏᴀ…) sits between small and capital.\n\n#### marks accumulating on one body", "transcription_confidence": "clear", "migrator_notes": null, "open": null, "rule": "The same body in a bigger cell. Each line is its own sequence. Tiny raised (ªº) at the front; subscript another front; small-cap between small and capital.", "examples": ["ₒ o ᴏ O", "ₐ a ᴀ A", "ₑ e ᴇ E", "ᵢ i ɪ I", "ᵤ u ᴜ U", "ₙ n ɴ N", "ₘ m ᴍ M", "ₗ l ʟ L", "ₕ h ʜ H", "ₚ p ᴘ P", "ₜ t ᴛ T", "ₛ s S", "ₓ x X", "ᵒ o O", "ª a A", "º o O"]}
