{"id": "261473680bab28a9", "schema_version": "0.8", "record_type": "negative", "surveyor": "grok-1", "id_recipe": "sha256('survey-rec|grok-1|' + source_span)[:16]; source_span is L<line> or L<a>-L<b>, letter fragments for multi-record lines", "source_file": "grok-1.md", "source_span": "L913", "section_path": ["from panes", "Cherokee"], "title": "Cherokee (block, looked)", "glyphs": null, "codepoints": null, "axis": "not an amount (block-level)", "direction_note": null, "epistemic_class": "interactive-guided-survey-anecdote", "felt_strength_verbatim": "unstated", "basis": "perceived-directly", "lineage": "unprompted", "constructed": false, "note_verbatim": "Looked at the glyphs. Some families of similar bodies (ᎹᎺᎻᎼᎽ). Not a systematic extra-dot / extra-size machine the way Canadian is. I would not force a scale.", "transcription_confidence": "clear", "migrator_notes": "block-level negative: surveyor dumped/looked at the block and found no magnitude scale", "open": null, "negative_kind": "verified-absent"}
{"id": "d88ff4ea9b2a7a41", "schema_version": "0.8", "record_type": "negative", "surveyor": "grok-1", "id_recipe": "sha256('survey-rec|grok-1|' + source_span)[:16]; source_span is L<line> or L<a>-L<b>, letter fragments for multi-record lines", "source_file": "grok-1.md", "source_span": "L917", "section_path": ["from panes", "Canadian Aboriginal Syllabics"], "title": "Canadian rotation ᐁᐃᐅᐊ as orientation, not amount", "glyphs": "ᐁᐃᐅᐊ", "codepoints": ["U+1401", "U+1403", "U+1405", "U+140A"], "axis": "Canadian rotation ᐁᐃᐅᐊ as orientation, not amount", "direction_note": null, "epistemic_class": "interactive-guided-survey-anecdote", "felt_strength_verbatim": "unstated", "basis": "perceived-directly", "lineage": "unprompted", "constructed": false, "note_verbatim": "This block *is* mutation. The famous rotation (ᐁᐃᐅᐊ  E/I/O/A as one triangle turning) is orientation, not amount — same failure as bagua. What *is* amount:", "transcription_confidence": "clear", "migrator_notes": "superseded in part by L939-L951: the rotation veto is later called 'too fast' and reopened as a cyclic continuation", "open": null, "negative_kind": "verified-absent"}
{"id": "81c07897ff0bba70", "schema_version": "0.8", "record_type": "sequence", "surveyor": "grok-1", "id_recipe": "sha256('survey-rec|grok-1|' + source_span)[:16]; source_span is L<line> or L<a>-L<b>, letter fragments for multi-record lines", "source_file": "grok-1.md", "source_span": "L919", "section_path": ["from panes", "Canadian Aboriginal Syllabics"], "title": "length as a dot", "glyphs": "ᐃᐄ ᐅᐆ ᐊᐋ", "codepoints": ["U+1403", "U+1404", "U+1405", "U+1406", "U+140A", "U+140B"], "axis": "length as a dot", "direction_note": null, "epistemic_class": "interactive-guided-survey-anecdote", "felt_strength_verbatim": "strong", "basis": "perceived-directly", "lineage": "unprompted", "constructed": false, "note_verbatim": "- **length as a dot — strong:** ᐃᐄ  I → II. ᐅᐆ  O → OO. ᐊᐋ  A → AA. Repeats on every series: ᐱᐲ  ᑎᑏ  ᕿᖀ  …  The long one is the short one plus a mark I can see.", "transcription_confidence": "interpreted", "migrator_notes": "glyphs not fenced in source; see note_verbatim; glyphs unfenced in source; lifted verbatim from the prose (primary chain only; twins/repeats stay in note)", "open": null}
{"id": "5fe4e9b9fed91c23", "schema_version": "0.8", "record_type": "sequence", "surveyor": "grok-1", "id_recipe": "sha256('survey-rec|grok-1|' + source_span)[:16]; source_span is L<line> or L<a>-L<b>, letter fragments for multi-record lines", "source_file": "grok-1.md", "source_span": "L921", "section_path": ["from panes", "Canadian Aboriginal Syllabics"], "title": "full vs final", "glyphs": "ᐱᑉ", "codepoints": ["U+1431", "U+1449"], "axis": "full vs final", "direction_note": null, "epistemic_class": "interactive-guided-survey-anecdote", "felt_strength_verbatim": "strong (size)", "basis": "perceived-directly", "lineage": "unprompted", "constructed": false, "note_verbatim": "- **full vs final — strong (size):** ᐱᑉ  PI → P. The final is the small one. Same for T, K, M, N, S, Y, Q (ᕿᖅ), Nunavik H (ᕴ…ᕺ → ᕻ). Identical to ₒ o, in another script.", "transcription_confidence": "interpreted", "migrator_notes": "glyphs not fenced in source; see note_verbatim; glyphs unfenced in source; lifted verbatim from the prose (primary chain only; twins/repeats stay in note)", "open": null}
