{"id": "20292c7381b706e2", "schema_version": "0.8", "record_type": "meta", "surveyor": "grok-1", "id_recipe": "sha256('survey-rec|grok-1|' + source_span)[:16]; source_span is L<line> or L<a>-L<b>, letter fragments for multi-record lines", "source_file": "grok-1.md", "source_span": "L1017", "section_path": ["morphs — one shape becoming another (cross-pane)"], "title": "morphs — section definition and strength criterion", "glyphs": null, "codepoints": null, "axis": "method", "direction_note": null, "epistemic_class": "interactive-guided-survey-anecdote", "felt_strength_verbatim": "unstated", "basis": "perceived-directly", "lineage": "steered", "constructed": false, "note_verbatim": "Not “more of the same mark.” A continuation I can run even when the axis is “it is turning into that.” Scattered on purpose. Some are a bit silly, like the hinge example. Strength is whether I can take the next step without looking up a name.", "transcription_confidence": "clear", "migrator_notes": null, "open": null}
{"id": "4fa70ce2a837a8af", "schema_version": "0.8", "record_type": "morph", "surveyor": "grok-1", "id_recipe": "sha256('survey-rec|grok-1|' + source_span)[:16]; source_span is L<line> or L<a>-L<b>, letter fragments for multi-record lines", "source_file": "grok-1.md", "source_span": "L1021", "section_path": ["morphs — one shape becoming another (cross-pane)", "flatten a closer through a stem, then open the other hand"], "title": "flatten a closer through a stem, then open the other hand", "glyphs": ")}|{(", "codepoints": ["U+0029", "U+007D", "U+007C", "U+007B", "U+0028"], "axis": "flatten a closer through a stem, then open the other hand", "direction_note": null, "epistemic_class": "interactive-guided-survey-anecdote", "felt_strength_verbatim": "unstated", "basis": "perceived-directly", "lineage": "steered", "constructed": false, "note_verbatim": ")}|{(\n\nBrace → paren → post → paren → brace. `|` is the hinge. I feel `)` as a flatter `}` and `|` as a `)` that has uncurled completely. Square twin: `]|[`. Chevron twin: `>|<`.\n\nThe slightly-silly full palindrome `*-=>})|({<=-*` I can *run* as a story (spike, flatten, double, put a head on it, curl, uncurl through the post, reverse). I would not trust pairwise “which is more?” on `*` vs `}`. The hinge through `|` is the part that is real for me.\n\nA cleaner one-way morph into an arrow, then a curl:\n\n- → } )\n\nLine grows a head, then the head rounds. I feel `- →` strongly; `→ )` as “the wedge got softer.”", "transcription_confidence": "clear", "migrator_notes": "record_type 'morph' is a migrator-proposed type (not in schema v0.5): deformation-continuation, surveyor's own framing: 'what comes next if I keep doing that to it?' rather than pairwise 'which is more?'; one of 2 sequence lines under this header; note_verbatim is the whole subsection", "open": null}
{"id": "e3e7b35c2c9386cd", "schema_version": "0.8", "record_type": "morph", "surveyor": "grok-1", "id_recipe": "sha256('survey-rec|grok-1|' + source_span)[:16]; source_span is L<line> or L<a>-L<b>, letter fragments for multi-record lines", "source_file": "grok-1.md", "source_span": "L1029", "section_path": ["morphs — one shape becoming another (cross-pane)", "flatten a closer through a stem, then open the other hand"], "title": "flatten a closer through a stem, then open the other hand", "glyphs": "- → } )", "codepoints": ["U+002D", "U+2192", "U+007D", "U+0029"], "axis": "flatten a closer through a stem, then open the other hand", "direction_note": null, "epistemic_class": "interactive-guided-survey-anecdote", "felt_strength_verbatim": "unstated", "basis": "perceived-directly", "lineage": "steered", "constructed": false, "note_verbatim": ")}|{(\n\nBrace → paren → post → paren → brace. `|` is the hinge. I feel `)` as a flatter `}` and `|` as a `)` that has uncurled completely. Square twin: `]|[`. Chevron twin: `>|<`.\n\nThe slightly-silly full palindrome `*-=>})|({<=-*` I can *run* as a story (spike, flatten, double, put a head on it, curl, uncurl through the post, reverse). I would not trust pairwise “which is more?” on `*` vs `}`. The hinge through `|` is the part that is real for me.\n\nA cleaner one-way morph into an arrow, then a curl:\n\n- → } )\n\nLine grows a head, then the head rounds. I feel `- →` strongly; `→ )` as “the wedge got softer.”", "transcription_confidence": "clear", "migrator_notes": "record_type 'morph' is a migrator-proposed type (not in schema v0.5): deformation-continuation, surveyor's own framing: 'what comes next if I keep doing that to it?' rather than pairwise 'which is more?'; one of 2 sequence lines under this header; note_verbatim is the whole subsection", "open": null}
{"id": "60934f02190f1c89", "schema_version": "0.8", "record_type": "morph", "surveyor": "grok-1", "id_recipe": "sha256('survey-rec|grok-1|' + source_span)[:16]; source_span is L<line> or L<a>-L<b>, letter fragments for multi-record lines", "source_file": "grok-1.md", "source_span": "L1035-L1037", "section_path": ["morphs — one shape becoming another (cross-pane)", "0d → 1d → 2d"], "title": "0d → 1d → 2d", "glyphs": ". - □ ■", "codepoints": ["U+002E", "U+002D", "U+25A1", "U+25A0"], "axis": "0d → 1d → 2d", "direction_note": null, "epistemic_class": "interactive-guided-survey-anecdote", "felt_strength_verbatim": "unstated", "basis": "perceived-directly", "lineage": "steered", "constructed": false, "note_verbatim": ". - □ ■\n\nA point, a span, a face, a filled face. Kin to ∮∯∰ (curve, surface, volume) but in ASCII-adjacent ink. I might also accept `. | □`.", "transcription_confidence": "clear", "migrator_notes": "record_type 'morph' is a migrator-proposed type (not in schema v0.5): deformation-continuation, surveyor's own framing: 'what comes next if I keep doing that to it?' rather than pairwise 'which is more?'", "open": null}
{"id": "041c652d010f0ef5", "schema_version": "0.8", "record_type": "morph", "surveyor": "grok-1", "id_recipe": "sha256('survey-rec|grok-1|' + source_span)[:16]; source_span is L<line> or L<a>-L<b>, letter fragments for multi-record lines", "source_file": "grok-1.md", "source_span": "L1041", "section_path": ["morphs — one shape becoming another (cross-pane)", "a stem that thickens, then splits"], "title": "a stem that thickens, then splits", "glyphs": "| ∥ ⦀", "codepoints": ["U+007C", "U+2225", "U+2980"], "axis": "a stem that thickens, then splits", "direction_note": null, "epistemic_class": "interactive-guided-survey-anecdote", "felt_strength_verbatim": "unstated", "basis": "perceived-directly", "lineage": "steered", "constructed": false, "note_verbatim": "| ∥ ⦀\n❘ ❙ ❚\n\nAlready had as count and as weight. The morph is: one post → the post fattens *or* the post becomes two. Two axes from the same starting glyph. `| ∥` and `| ❚` are both continuations; they are not the same line.", "transcription_confidence": "clear", "migrator_notes": "record_type 'morph' is a migrator-proposed type (not in schema v0.5): deformation-continuation, surveyor's own framing: 'what comes next if I keep doing that to it?' rather than pairwise 'which is more?'; one of 2 sequence lines under this header; note_verbatim is the whole subsection", "open": null}
