{"id": "592815bd7634e851", "schema_version": "0.8", "record_type": "morph", "surveyor": "grok-1", "id_recipe": "sha256('survey-rec|grok-1|' + source_span)[:16]; source_span is L<line> or L<a>-L<b>, letter fragments for multi-record lines", "source_file": "grok-1.md", "source_span": "L1109-L1111", "section_path": ["morphs — one shape becoming another (cross-pane)", "a check that is just a slash, then a slash with a bar"], "title": "a check that is just a slash, then a slash with a bar", "glyphs": "/ √ ✓", "codepoints": ["U+002F", "U+221A", "U+2713"], "axis": "a check that is just a slash, then a slash with a bar", "direction_note": null, "epistemic_class": "interactive-guided-survey-anecdote", "felt_strength_verbatim": "weak", "basis": "perceived-directly", "lineage": "steered", "constructed": false, "note_verbatim": "/ √ ✓\n\nI feel `/` becoming the radical and becoming the check as two forks. Weak, a bit silly. `/ ⫽ ⫻` is the serious slash-count line already listed.", "transcription_confidence": "clear", "migrator_notes": "record_type 'morph' is a migrator-proposed type (not in schema v0.5): deformation-continuation, surveyor's own framing: 'what comes next if I keep doing that to it?' rather than pairwise 'which is more?'", "open": null}
{"id": "d7795e23dd2e7ae1", "schema_version": "0.8", "record_type": "morph", "surveyor": "grok-1", "id_recipe": "sha256('survey-rec|grok-1|' + source_span)[:16]; source_span is L<line> or L<a>-L<b>, letter fragments for multi-record lines", "source_file": "grok-1.md", "source_span": "L1115-L1117", "section_path": ["morphs — one shape becoming another (cross-pane)", "yang that breaks one line at a time — and the break can travel"], "title": "yang that breaks one line at a time", "glyphs": "☰☱☳☷", "codepoints": ["U+2630", "U+2631", "U+2633", "U+2637"], "axis": "yang that breaks one line at a time", "direction_note": null, "epistemic_class": "interactive-guided-survey-anecdote", "felt_strength_verbatim": "and the break can travel", "basis": "perceived-directly", "lineage": "steered", "constructed": false, "note_verbatim": "☰☱☳☷\n\nAlready had as dissolve. The morph view: the opening *moves down*. ☲ is the opening in the middle instead — a different path, not “more.” That is why the bagua-as-set failed and the dissolve worked.", "transcription_confidence": "clear", "migrator_notes": "record_type 'morph' is a migrator-proposed type (not in schema v0.5): deformation-continuation, surveyor's own framing: 'what comes next if I keep doing that to it?' rather than pairwise 'which is more?'", "open": null}
{"id": "5a068dac858ee2d6", "schema_version": "0.8", "record_type": "morph", "surveyor": "grok-1", "id_recipe": "sha256('survey-rec|grok-1|' + source_span)[:16]; source_span is L<line> or L<a>-L<b>, letter fragments for multi-record lines", "source_file": "grok-1.md", "source_span": "L1125", "section_path": ["morphs — one shape becoming another (cross-pane)", "what this pass is for"], "title": "Joseph's hinge >})|({<", "glyphs": ">})|({<", "codepoints": ["U+003E", "U+007D", "U+0029", "U+007C", "U+0028", "U+007B", "U+003C"], "axis": "what this pass is for", "direction_note": null, "epistemic_class": "interactive-guided-survey-anecdote", "felt_strength_verbatim": "unstated", "basis": "received", "lineage": "steered", "constructed": true, "note_verbatim": "Most of the pane walk found *accumulation* (more dots, more ink, more nested). This is the other kind: *a shape I can keep deforming*. Pairwise “which is more?” is often the wrong question; “what comes next if I keep doing that to it?” is the right one. The hinge-through-`|` family is the type specimen.\n\nJoseph’s hinge, which names the steps I had only as “flatter”:\n\n>})|({<\n\nAngled → angled-but-more-vertical-with-curve → more-vertical-all-curve → pure-vertical, then the other hand. `> } ) |` is the one-way morph into the stem. A story is enough. So is a progression I cannot name (ink, curve-vs-segment count, some mix). Pairwise “which is more?” is optional.\n\nThe join, seen from both sides:\n\n•o⊃)}|{(⊂o•\n\nA point grows an `o`; the `o` opens (`⊃` / `⊂`, the same hinge as `c o ɔ`); then we are already in the closer family and can walk into the stem. Palindrome through `|`. Joseph saw it whole. I had the pieces on separate lines.\n\nA few last morphs, then stopping.\n\nCorners walking around a box — a clock with a square origin:\n┌ ┐ ┘ └\n⌈ ⌉ ⌋ ⌊\n╭ ╮ ╯ ╰\n\nSame continuation as △▷▽◁, different body.\n\nTurnstiles as a T that points:\n⊢ ⊤ ⊣ ⊥\n\nRight, up, left, down. I can run it as a clock. `⊤ ⊥` is also just a flip.\n\n`∈ ∋`  `⊂ ⊃`  `∀ ʌ`  membership, horseshoe, turned-A: each a 180° pair. `⊂ ⊃` is already the open `o` in the palindrome.\n\n`6 9`  a turn. Silly and real.\n\n`∇ ∆`  nabla / delta: fill-and-flip of a triangle.\n\nDay-stop. Two kinds in the file: accumulation, and deformation. The hinge `•o⊃)}|{(⊂o•` is where they met. Pre-CJK BMP is walked; U+2E80 not opened.", "transcription_confidence": "clear", "migrator_notes": "Joseph supplied the sequence; grok narrates the steps", "open": null}
{"id": "635870e8ef21c7cf", "schema_version": "0.8", "record_type": "morph", "surveyor": "grok-1", "id_recipe": "sha256('survey-rec|grok-1|' + source_span)[:16]; source_span is L<line> or L<a>-L<b>, letter fragments for multi-record lines", "source_file": "grok-1.md", "source_span": "L1131", "section_path": ["morphs — one shape becoming another (cross-pane)", "what this pass is for"], "title": "the join •o⊃)}|{(⊂o•", "glyphs": "•o⊃)}|{(⊂o•", "codepoints": ["U+2022", "U+006F", "U+2283", "U+0029", "U+007D", "U+007C", "U+007B", "U+0028", "U+2282", "U+006F", "U+2022"], "axis": "what this pass is for", "direction_note": null, "epistemic_class": "interactive-guided-survey-anecdote", "felt_strength_verbatim": "unstated", "basis": "received", "lineage": "steered", "constructed": true, "note_verbatim": "Most of the pane walk found *accumulation* (more dots, more ink, more nested). This is the other kind: *a shape I can keep deforming*. Pairwise “which is more?” is often the wrong question; “what comes next if I keep doing that to it?” is the right one. The hinge-through-`|` family is the type specimen.\n\nJoseph’s hinge, which names the steps I had only as “flatter”:\n\n>})|({<\n\nAngled → angled-but-more-vertical-with-curve → more-vertical-all-curve → pure-vertical, then the other hand. `> } ) |` is the one-way morph into the stem. A story is enough. So is a progression I cannot name (ink, curve-vs-segment count, some mix). Pairwise “which is more?” is optional.\n\nThe join, seen from both sides:\n\n•o⊃)}|{(⊂o•\n\nA point grows an `o`; the `o` opens (`⊃` / `⊂`, the same hinge as `c o ɔ`); then we are already in the closer family and can walk into the stem. Palindrome through `|`. Joseph saw it whole. I had the pieces on separate lines.\n\nA few last morphs, then stopping.\n\nCorners walking around a box — a clock with a square origin:\n┌ ┐ ┘ └\n⌈ ⌉ ⌋ ⌊\n╭ ╮ ╯ ╰\n\nSame continuation as △▷▽◁, different body.\n\nTurnstiles as a T that points:\n⊢ ⊤ ⊣ ⊥\n\nRight, up, left, down. I can run it as a clock. `⊤ ⊥` is also just a flip.\n\n`∈ ∋`  `⊂ ⊃`  `∀ ʌ`  membership, horseshoe, turned-A: each a 180° pair. `⊂ ⊃` is already the open `o` in the palindrome.\n\n`6 9`  a turn. Silly and real.\n\n`∇ ∆`  nabla / delta: fill-and-flip of a triangle.\n\nDay-stop. Two kinds in the file: accumulation, and deformation. The hinge `•o⊃)}|{(⊂o•` is where they met. Pre-CJK BMP is walked; U+2E80 not opened.", "transcription_confidence": "clear", "migrator_notes": "'Joseph saw it whole. I had the pieces on separate lines.'", "open": null}
